    {
      "type": "grammar",
      "title": "<ico-book></ico-book> there is/are · can · preposiciones",
      "intro": "En español «hay» sirve para uno o varios. En inglés cambia: <b>there is</b> (uno) y <b>there are</b> (varios). Con <b>can</b> pides cosas, y las preposiciones dicen dónde está cada lugar.",
      "parts": [
        {
          "type": "phrases",
          "items": [
            {
              "en": "There is a bank near here.",
              "sp": "Hay un banco cerca. — uno: <b>there is</b>."
            },
            {
              "en": "There are two cafés on this street.",
              "sp": "Hay dos cafés en esta calle. — varios: <b>there are</b>."
            },
            {
              "en": "Is there a pharmacy near here?",
              "sp": "¿Hay una farmacia cerca? — Yes, there is. / No, there isn't."
            },
            {
              "en": "The bank is next to the café.",
              "sp": "El banco está al lado del café."
            },
            {
              "en": "Go straight and turn left.",
              "sp": "Sigue derecho y dobla a la izquierda. — turn right = a la derecha."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "cells",
          "cells": [
            {
              "h": "there is / there are",
              "body": "<code>There is</code> a bank. (uno)<br><code>There are</code> two cafés. (varios)<br><span class=\"es\">Is there…? · Are there…?</span>"
            },
            {
              "h": "can (pedido / habilidad)",
              "body": "<code>Can I have…?</code> (pedido)<br><code>Can you help me?</code><br>I <code>can</code> speak Spanish. (habilidad)"
            },
            {
              "h": "preposiciones de lugar",
              "body": "in <span class=\"es\">(en)</span> · on <span class=\"es\">(sobre/en)</span> · next to <span class=\"es\">(al lado de)</span> · behind <span class=\"es\">(detrás)</span> · near <span class=\"es\">(cerca)</span>"
            },
            {
              "h": "ejemplo",
              "body": "<span class=\"ok\">The bank is next to the café.</span><br><span class=\"ok\">It's on Main Street.</span>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "note",
          "gold": true,
          "body": "<b>«Hay» no siempre es there is.</b> <s class='x'>There is two banks.</s> → <span class='ok'>There are two banks.</span> Y para pedir, la pregunta suena mejor que la orden: <s class='x'>I want a coffee.</s> → <span class='ok'>Can I have a coffee, please?</span>"
        },
